kely than an Aussie one.|The Aussie's jobs hit keeps pressure on this bullish view, even though the loonie offered no help overnight.|The yen slipped on softer inflation, and this quiet stand-off tipped into a kiwi lean in the shadow.|A true risk-off close puts this kiwi lean on shaky ground ahead of Friday's measurement.|Two quiet commodity currencies, and the kiwi still holds the better hand.|The yen's soft inflation cut away the support under this bearish view, and the shadow now shows a stand-off.|Still a stand-off on the scores, but a risk-off regime tonight could break it toward the franc.|Japan's softer core inflation pulled the yen down, and this bearish lean drifted into a stand-off.|Gold kept sliding through a stock-market rout, so the haven story has not saved it yet.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED (strengthened)~Stocks fell 2% but December hike odds held near 96%; Barr: inflation too high.|CONFIRMED~No spread print after 156.3bp (17 Nov); Senate budget (PLF) debate opens today.|WEAKENED (watch)~No BoE item overnight; UK retail sales at 09:00 are the next test.|WEAKENED (watch)~Core CPI 2.2% vs 2.3% expected (second soft surprise after GDP): shadow −2; 0 if read as in line.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~VIX closed about 28.4: the franc condition is met on a close; score re-measured from Friday closes.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~No Canadian item overnight; retail sales at 15:30 Bucharest.|INVALIDATED (bearish direction)~Jobs-miss condition still met; shadow +3 central, 0 if the RBA outlook (R2) is cut.|CONFIRMED~No New Zealand item overnight; most exposed to a −2 risk regime at Friday close.|CONFIRMED (fragile)~Gold factor −3 unchanged (spot near $3,675); XAU shadow +3 only via the USD shadow.")
