    array.push(cH, "A record-style Wall Street rebound did not rescue the euro's side of this call.|Pill talked tough in Vienna, but cable's bearish read did not budge.|Risk appetite roared back, and that is the yen's weak spot in this matchup.|Fear eased a lot today, but not quite enough to strip the franc's shelter role.|Oil slipped again on a risk-on day, and the loonie stays the weakest link.|The Aussie got the risk-on rally it needed, and that puts this bearish call under pressure.|The kiwi now has two written strength signals in one day.|Germany hummed, France stumbled, and Pill sounded firm: EURGBP still reads zero.|A risk-on Monday tilts the yen's cushion away, but EURJPY stays near even.|Calmer markets help the euro here, though the VIX is not yet under 25.|The Aussie's risk-on boost meets a flat euro, and the zero gap holds.|The kiwi adds a risk-on tailwind to its retail surprise; EURNZD stays two-sided.|Cheaper oil keeps doing the heavy lifting for this bullish +7.|Pill's firm words and a risk-on surge both lean against the yen; still +1.|A calmer market narrows the franc's advantage, but the pair stays at zero.|Both sides got a little help today, so GBPAUD stays level at zero.|The kiwi had the better Monday, and GBPNZD's small tilt looks thinner.|Oil's slide keeps the loonie down, and the +7 tilt to sterling holds.|The classic risk barometer swung toward the Aussie today, but the score is still +1.|Carry beat shelter on Monday, though the gap stays at zero.|Both antipodeans enjoyed the rally, so AUDNZD stays two-sided at +2.|The Aussie gains a risk-on tailwind while oil falls again: +7 could get stronger.|The kiwi gained two tailwinds, and the yen lost its shelter: still −1 on paper.|Risk-on helps the kiwi against the franc, but the pair stays two-sided at −2.|Kiwi up, oil down: this +5 could get even stronger.|Wall Street's rally meets the yen's written weakening condition: this bearish call is under pressure.|The VIX fell to about 27, close to the 25 line that would weaken the franc's leg.|Two havens lost fear premium together; CHFJPY stays at +1.|Gold jumped about 4% on a risk-on day, but its score stays at +1.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED~Fed December hike still 96% priced; soft US services PMI (54.7 vs 55.7) is MEDIUM, no score effect.|CONFIRMED~Euro-area flash composite flat at 51.7; France 46.2 vs 48.1 expected (MEDIUM); oil lower again helps the importer.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Pill: 'we do need to take action now' (no December reference); UK flash output 52.3 from 52.9, so the strong-PMI condition is not met.|INVALIDATED (bearish direction)~Written yen-weakening condition 'a sharp risk-on rebound' met intraday (S&P +5%, VIX 27); Tokyo closed; shadow unchanged.|WEAKENED (watch)~VIX fell to 27 from 35.9: no longer above 30, not yet under the 25 line of the franc-weakening condition.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~WTI $81 and Brent $88 (down 3–4%) on a risk-on day; no written US–Canada deal; Macklem Tue 19:40.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Written Aussie strength condition 'risk-on rebound' met intraday; CPI Wed 02:30 pending; shadow unchanged.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Carried from the morning (retail +2.2% vs +0.5%), now joined by the risk-on rebound; shadow unchanged (MEDIUM release).|CONFIRMED~Gold $3,663 (+4.2%) is price context only; no ETF, central-bank or real-yield data; G +1.")
