    array.push(cD, "C-7,C-7,S8,C7,C14,P-7,P-9,T0,T1,T0,T0,T2,C7,T1,T0,T0,T2,C7,T1,T0,T2,S7,T-1,T-2,S5,P-6,W-7,T1,T1")
    array.push(cH, "The rally held into the close, yet the dollar side of EURUSD never lost its grip.|Cable woke up to the same story it went to bed with: firm Fed, quiet Bank of England.|Tokyo came back from its holiday to a risk-on world, and the yen stayed soft.|Fear cooled further, but the VIX closed above 25, so the franc keeps a little shelter.|Crude lost another 4% into the close, so the widest gap on the board stays wide.|The Aussie's risk-on condition is now met on a close, but the currency itself barely bounced.|The kiwi kept both of Monday's strength signals, though the dollar leg still dominates.|A quiet night for both sides, and EURGBP stays balanced at zero.|Cheaper oil helps both importers again, so EURJPY stays close to even.|The VIX closed near 26.6, so the franc's shelter is thinner but not gone.|The Aussie got its risk-on close, the euro got nothing new: still zero.|The kiwi's two tailwinds survived the night, keeping EURNZD's euro tilt thin.|Oil's fourth-percent drop did the work again for this bullish +7.|Risk-on held into the close, a mild headwind for the yen; GBPJPY still +1.|Fear faded, the BoE stayed silent, and GBPCHF stays at zero.|The Aussie's strength trigger is met, but GBPAUD's gap is still flat.|The kiwi's improvement holds, trimming the pound's small edge in GBPNZD.|Oil slid again into the close, keeping the pound's +7 advantage intact.|Both legs' risk-on conditions are now met on a close, but AUDJPY's score is still +1.|Carry beat shelter again overnight, though AUDCHF stays at zero.|Both antipodeans enjoyed a risk-on close, so AUDNZD stays at +2.|Risk-on for the Aussie, another oil drop for the loonie: this +7 leans stronger.|The kiwi's tailwinds and the yen's fading shelter both held: still −1 on paper.|A calmer close helps the kiwi against the franc; the gap stays −2.|Kiwi steady, oil down again: this +5 could get even stronger.|The yen-weakening condition is now met on a close, so this bearish call stays under pressure.|The VIX closed around 26.6, close to but above the 25 line that would weaken the franc.|Two havens lost shelter demand together; CHFJPY stays at +1.|Gold added about 2.7% on Monday, but its fundamental score stays at +1.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED~December Fed hike 95–96% priced after Monday's equity surge; 2-year 4.70%; no Fed voice turned patient.|CONFIRMED~No CMP deal or spread print; Macron's fiscal golden-rule idea is context only; oil lower again helps the importer.|CONFIRMED (watch)~No MPC remarks since Pill; Greene 14:30 is the next test; equities rebounded, the opposite of the weakening condition.|INVALIDATED (bearish direction)~Yen-weakening condition 'sharp risk-on rebound' now met on a close (S&P +4.7%); Tokyo reopened, no MoF comment; shadow unchanged.|WEAKENED (watch)~VIX closed 26.6 (from 35.9): not above 30, not yet under the 25 line of the franc-weakening condition.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~WTI −4.5% to $80, Brent $89 on the Iran-strike pause; no written US–Canada deal; Macklem 19:40.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Aussie 'risk-on rebound' condition met on the close, but AUDUSD near an 11-month low with cuts priced; CPI Wed 02:30.|INVALIDATED (bullish direction)~Carried: strong Q3 retail plus a risk-on close; no NZ news overnight; shadow unchanged (MEDIUM release).|CONFIRMED~Gold +2.7% to $3,635 is price context only; no ETF, central-bank or real-yield data; G +1.")
